A||||5||BAM-BAM||Is there any thing I should know?||||5||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||03-25-2000||10:20 PM||||Hey guys, highly technical stuff here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">I am<BR>replacing my IAC valve and i was wondering if there is anything that I should know or be aware of. Do they have a breakin sequence?<BR>Is there a trick to get them to seat right? anything. I know it sounds lame, but, what the heck. After all there's no such thing as a stupid question.....Right? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR> Thanx, BAM-BAM <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||WisconsinGT||03-25-2000||11:15 PM||||Bam-Bam, I just replaced mine. I put in a new GM IAC Valve. It is quite easy. After unpacking I noticed that the pindel was pushed in all the way. (Make sure yours is before the install.) Then put it in. You might want to clean out the area that it goes into. Alot of crud builds up inside that part of the throttle body. After you tighten the IAC Valve, (Do not over tighten it.) start your Fiero, (It will idle high thats O.K.) and drive it around for awhile. The idle will go down after the pindle sets. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||03-25-2000||11:46 PM||||use some carb clean that is 02 safe<BR>aka oxygen sensor safe, it should say it on the back someplace,  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||03-26-2000||12:03 AM||||  Wisconsin, are you saying to make sure the pindle "IS" pushed in befor the install? Sorry another dumb question <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>  Thanx, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierodave||03-26-2000||12:59 AM||||Bam BAM<BR>just take out the old one and make sure the new one is retracted further then the old one, <BR>if not you will wreck the new one!  pull the old one out, it will be easy to tell!!!  most new ones are retracted<BR>FD<BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 03-26-2000).]||||reg||1
